so we have a bit of a light-hearted  story to wrap things up today and it has  to do with one of the worst pandemic  inspired changes to our society which is  of course the dreaded qr code at  restaurants replacing physical menus we  know that during the pandemic businesses  would try to take advantage of the  situation by not providing us with  things that we were used to and just  using kobat as an excuse like they would  say oh sorry we can't clean your hotel  room because of kovid and sorry you  can't bring your reusable bag to the  grocery store because of cobit remember  that one well none of these changes were  as bad as the dreaded qr code scanner at  restaurants and while some of the  pandemic era inconveniences are no more  the dreaded qr code at restaurants  persist and the idea of introducing them  in the first place was pretty clear you  don't have people touching the menus  that way you don't have to sanitize the  menus as often and it's the same reason  why restaurants during the height of the  pandemic got rid of the ketchup bottles  on the tables and the salt and pepper  shakers and it didn't take long for us  to learn that the virus was largely an  airborne transmitted virus it didn't  really transfer that much from surfaces  so a lot of these changes that we made  were pointless and we could have  backtracked on them right then and there  pretty early on in the pandemic but  restaurants persisted with the qr thing  because printing menus can be expensive  you need to replace them sometimes when  they get dirty or when you change the  menu you got to think about the printing  costs and it's also in a low labor  environment just better for businesses  to have the qr codes because you don't  have to have staff distribute and  collect the menus but customers  absolutely revile the qr code myself  included a recent technomic survey found  that about 88 of respondents said that  they preferred paper menus to digital qr  codes about 66 percent of respondents  agreed or strongly agreed that they  didn't like qr codes because they  involve pulling out your phone as soon  as you sit down at the table about 57  agreed that using qr codes felt like a  chore and 55 agreed that qr codes were  hard to read and browse through and it  actually does seem to make sense for  restaurants to bring back the physical  menus now not just because customers  hate it and they'll sometimes leave  these awful reviews for restaurants  because of the qr codes the qr codes  actually are leading to people ordering  less because if you have a menu left on  the table for example sometimes it'll  have the pictures of the food and the  drinks and the desserts and everything  so you may be tempted to order more just  by giving a glance over at it and saying  oh that looks good i want to order that  whereas if you have to pull out your  phone scan the qr code open up the  website scroll down find what you're  looking for that's more of an active  action versus a passive action of just  glancing at something and saying that  looks good i want that now depending on  my mood i will sometimes lie at the  restaurant and i'll say i don't have a  phone or i have a flip phone and so i  need a physical menu that is something  that you can try out at home there  they'll have a few physical menus at  their ready so they're probably not  going to be happy to give it to you but  you can always just make up an excuse  and i'm sure you'll get it and another  pro tip for dealing with the other  inconvenience that people absolutely  hate at restaurants is when you're about  to pay for the meal just have cash handy  with the tip included so that when the  server comes over you can just pay for  it all at once they bring you the check  you look at the amount you probably know  about what it's going to be you just  give them the cash they go on with it  rather than having to give them a card  they leave come back and then you fill  out the tip and everything it saves you  about half the headache because that's  one of the things that people hate most  about restaurants having to wait at the  end of your meal when you just want to  get up and leave all right that's going  to do it for today's show my thank you  to david for allowing me to fill in for  him today while he is traveling up in  montreal and we're going to have farron  cousins fill in the next couple of days  david will be back on thursday and  friday to finish out the week and if you  want more of the david pakman show be  sure to check out today's bonus show  which you can access by signing up for a  membership at joinpacman.com  or contributing to patreon at the five  dollar level at patreon.com  davidpakmanshow i'll see you on the bona  show

